WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
A clinical conversation carries more than words.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Prosody, pauses, accent, roles and non-speech cues
are part of the interaction.

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.000
A plain transcript does not carry
all of that acoustic evidence.

4
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Useful voice cues can also identify someone.
Privacy and preservation must be considered together.

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
AegisVox separates two interventions:
voice identity and identifying words.

6
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Assign one consistent reference voice
to each speaker.

7
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:38.000
SeedVC transforms voice identity
across every speaker and every turn.

8
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Plan consistent replacements for names,
locations and dates using the transcript context.

9
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Render affected complete turns with F5-TTS.
Other turns keep their converted audio.

10
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:59.000
Reconstruct the conversation
from edited and converted turns.

11
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Evaluate stages separately: speaker linkage,
lexical outcomes and clinical preservation.

12
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Matched edited-turn realization: 453/601 versus 535/601.
GPT-5.4 transcript judgments, not complete privacy.

13
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:18.000
Factorized privacy. Stage-resolved evaluation.
Speech is more than its transcript.
